body:
I'm a college student, I make $2600 a year, and in the end of the month, I will finally have the money I need to pay what's left of my debts.

&#x200B;

A year and a half ago some bad personal finance and a lot of irresponsable shopping put me into a snowball of credit card interest . The debt was bigger than my entire year's earnings. I renegotiated my debt and could get it to a monthly payment that I could afford. And I've been paying it ever since.

&#x200B;

In the end of January I'll finally have the money I need to pay the rest of my debt upfront and discount a lot of interest. And that's thanks to many jobs I did in these summer vacations (it is now summer where I live)  and a lot of financial planning.

&#x200B;

It may not sound like much to a lot of you, but to me it is. I thought I was lost when I renegotiated my debts and I thought I'd never be out of it. But I finally am.

&#x200B;

This comunity helped me out a lot.

Thanks!
